      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Logic Question:** When `skip_image_offset` is true, we shift `offset` by `current_image_offset`. At line 662, we validated `offset + size \u003c\u003d current_frame_size`. When we re-validate here with `sizeof(fp_buffer)`, we only ensure we do not read past the physical buffer capacity.\n\nHowever, because `adjusted_offset \u003d offset + current_image_offset`, the final read can span up to `current_frame_size + current_image_offset`. This means the host could potentially request to read uninitialized memory past the end of the valid `current_frame_size` bounds (but still within `fp_buffer`). \n\nShould this validation check `validate_fp_buffer_offset(current_frame_size, adjusted_offset, size)` instead of `sizeof(fp_buffer)` to ensure the host only reads valid frame bytes?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "f41b5e23175c0077bf001387d8f846ef3385155f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
